  "statuteText": "656:16 Uniformity; Folding. –\n\nThere shall be no impression or mark to distinguish one general election ballot from another. The names of all candidates shall be printed in uniform type, and the ballots for each town and city shall be such that their width and length when folded shall be uniform."
}
